<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Organization on STEP Batch 12</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/tags/organization/</link><description>Recent content in Organization on STEP Batch 12</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en_US</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:26:21 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://step-12.github.io/tags/organization/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Worldly Woes</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/worldlywoes/</link><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:15:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/worldlywoes/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="the-woes-of-the-world"&gt;The Woes Of The World&lt;a class="anchor" href="#the-woes-of-the-world"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;When we started writing Raylib programs, I gave you a template that used a &lt;code&gt;world&lt;/code&gt; object.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The idea was simple. We needed a way to share information between &lt;code&gt;setup()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;update()&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;draw()&lt;/code&gt;. So &lt;code&gt;setup()&lt;/code&gt; would create a world, and the other functions would use it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This was a reasonable idea.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, the world has grown in power. It now knows everything, goes everywhere, and is invited to functions that have absolutely no business meeting it.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Template</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/template/</link><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/template/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="modules-and-a-raylib-template"&gt;Modules and a Raylib Template&lt;a class="anchor" href="#modules-and-a-raylib-template"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;So far, each Raylib program you have written has lived in a single file.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We have already started organizing that file into functions:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;while&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;WindowShouldClose&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This gives different parts of the program different responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;But there is another kind of organization available to us.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We can separate our program into &lt;strong&gt;different files&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Skeleton</title><link>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/skeleton/</link><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://step-12.github.io/posts/raylib/skeleton/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="organizing-a-raylib-program"&gt;Organizing a Raylib Program&lt;a class="anchor" href="#organizing-a-raylib-program"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have now written a few small Raylib programs.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You have probably noticed that even a small program starts to contain several different kinds of code:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that prepares the window&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that changes things&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that draws things&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;code that keeps the program running&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It is useful to give these different responsibilities a little structure.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;We are going to use the following skeleton:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-js" data-lang="js"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;draw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is not a rule imposed by Raylib.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>